{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedInsertion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedInsertion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Multiset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":102,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowsSorted_getD_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowsSorted_getD_le","kind":"theorem","line":1381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1381-L1399","doc":"**General weak-row monotonicity (`getD` form).**  Within a row, entries\nweakly increase — the `row_weak'` obligation of a Mathlib SSYT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_getD_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_getD_lt","kind":"theorem","line":1373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1373-L1379","doc":"**General column strictness (`getD` form).**  For any `i1 < i2`, the entry\nabove is strictly smaller — the `col_strict'` obligation of a Mathlib SSYT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_getD_lt_aux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_getD_lt_aux","kind":"theorem","line":1347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1347-L1371","doc":"Auxiliary: strictness across a gap `d + 1`, by induction on `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_len_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_len_le","kind":"theorem","line":1334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1334-L1345","doc":"**Row lengths weakly decrease down a column-strict tableau.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":1318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1318-L1332","doc":"**Adjacent `StrictBelow` in `getD` form.**  Consecutive rows of a\ncolumn-strict tableau satisfy `StrictBelow`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_row_past","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_row_past","kind":"theorem","line":1313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1313-L1316","doc":"Row lookup past the end is the empty row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_row_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_row_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1308-L1311","doc":"Row lookup as an indexed entry (in range). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_standard","kind":"theorem","line":1288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1288-L1297","doc":"**`Q(w)` is a standard tableau.**  Rows and columns strictly increase, and\nthe entries are exactly the step indices `0 … |w| − 1` (bounded by\n`insertWordRec_entries_lt`; the cell count `|Q(w)| = |w|` follows from\n`insertWordRec_shape_eq_P` + `insertWord_totalCells`).  Together with\n`insertWord_rowsSorted` + `insertWord_colStrict` making `P(w)` semistandard,\nthis completes the `(P, Q)` pair the RSK bijection is built from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":1280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1280-L1286","doc":"**`Q(w)` has strictly increasing columns.**  The remaining half of\nstandardness: reading any column of the recording tableau top to bottom gives\na strictly increasing sequence of step indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":1263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1263-L1278","doc":"The recording fold preserves `Q` column-strictness, threading `ColStrict`\non both `P` and `Q` plus the monotone invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":1248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1248-L1261","doc":"**`insertRec` preserves column-strictness of `Q`.**  Combines the two halves:\nthe shape (Young) half transfers from `insert P x` (`insert_colStrict`) via\nthe `P`/`Q` shape agreement, and the value half is `insertRec_snd_colValStrict`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_colValStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_colValStrict","kind":"theorem","line":1160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1160-L1246","doc":"**`insertRec` preserves column value-strictness of `Q`.**  Given the result\nshape is a Young diagram (`ColShapeYoung`, supplied from the `P` side), each\nfreshly-written step-`s` cell sits below an older (smaller) entry, so columns\nstrictly increase.  The append and cascade cases mirror the `rowsStrict`\nproof, with the Young shape supplying `q1.length < qh.length` at the new\ncell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_headD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_headD","kind":"theorem","line":1144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1144-L1158","doc":"The head Q-row after `insertRec` is either the old head row or that row with\nthe step index appended. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":1134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1134-L1142","doc":"The Q-component of `insertRec` is never empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_append_end","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_append_end","kind":"theorem","line":1128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1128-L1132","doc":"`getD` at the join index of `l1 ++ [s]` reads the appended `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_append_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_append_lt","kind":"theorem","line":1123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1123-L1126","doc":"`getD` in the left part of an append. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colValStrict_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colValStrict_tail","kind":"theorem","line":1116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1116-L1121","doc":"`ColValStrict` passes to the tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colShapeYoung_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colShapeYoung_tail","kind":"theorem","line":1109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1109-L1114","doc":"`ColShapeYoung` passes to the tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_shapeYoung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_shapeYoung","kind":"theorem","line":1105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1105-L1107","doc":"`ColStrict` implies its shape half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colShapeYoung_of_shape_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colShapeYoung_of_shape_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1099,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1099-L1103","doc":"`ColShapeYoung` transfers across equal shapes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colShapeYoung_iff_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colShapeYoung_iff_shape","kind":"theorem","line":1092,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1092-L1097","doc":"`ColShapeYoung` reads only row lengths, so it is exactly a chain condition on\nthe shape list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_iff","kind":"theorem","line":1086,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1086-L1090","doc":"**`ColStrict` decomposes** into the shape (Young) and value (strict) halves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isChain_and","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isChain_and","kind":"theorem","line":1076,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1076-L1084","doc":"`IsChain` of a pointwise conjunction splits into a conjunction of `IsChain`s. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ColValStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ColValStrict","kind":"def","line":1071,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1071-L1074","doc":"Value half of `StrictBelow`: over the in-range positions, each column entry\nstrictly exceeds the one directly above it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ColShapeYoung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ColShapeYoung","kind":"def","line":1066,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1066-L1069","doc":"Shape half of `StrictBelow`: consecutive rows have weakly-decreasing lengths\n(the tableau shape is a Young diagram). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_entries_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_entries_lt","kind":"theorem","line":1042,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1042-L1049","doc":"**Every entry of `Q(w)` is `< |w|`.**  Combined with the cell count\n`|Q(w)| = |w|` (`insertWordRec_shape_eq_P` + `insertWord_totalCells`), the\nrecording tableau's entries are the step indices `0 … |w| − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_rowsStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_rowsStrict","kind":"theorem","line":1033,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1033-L1040","doc":"**`Q(w)` has strictly increasing rows.**  Half of standardness: reading any\nrow of the recording tableau left to right gives a strictly increasing\nsequence of step indices, because each cell records the (strictly larger)\nstep at which it was appended. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_rowsStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_rowsStrict","kind":"theorem","line":1019,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1019-L1031","doc":"The recording fold preserves row-strictness of `Q`, threading the monotone\ninvariant through each step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_allLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_allLt","kind":"theorem","line":1006,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L1006-L1017","doc":"The recording fold advances the entry bound by the word length: after\ninserting `w` starting at step `s`, every `Q` entry is `< s + |w|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_rowsStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_rowsStrict","kind":"theorem","line":965,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L965-L1004","doc":"**`insertRec` preserves row-strictness of `Q`.**  A no-bump appends the step\nindex `s` to the head row; since `s` exceeds every entry (the monotone\ninvariant), the row stays strictly increasing.  A bump leaves the head row\nuntouched and cascades. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sorted_lt_append_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sorted_lt_append_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":950,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L950-L963","doc":"Appending a strictly-larger element to a strictly-sorted list keeps it\nstrictly sorted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_allLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_allLt","kind":"theorem","line":916,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L916-L948","doc":"**The monotone invariant.**  If every entry of `Q` is `< s`, then after\nwriting step `s` every entry of the new `Q` is `< s + 1`: the old entries are\n`< s < s + 1`, and the single new cell holds `s < s + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.headD_mem_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.headD_mem_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":908,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L908-L914","doc":"If an entry lies in the head row `Q.headD []`, that row is genuinely in `Q`\n(it is nonempty, so `Q ≠ []`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_some","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_some","kind":"theorem","line":900,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L900-L906","doc":"The Q-component of a bumping `insertRec` keeps the head Q-row and cascades\ninto the tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_none","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_snd_none","kind":"theorem","line":893,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L893-L898","doc":"The Q-component of a no-bump `insertRec` appends the step index to the head\nQ-row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.RowsStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.RowsStrict","kind":"def","line":890,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L890-L891","doc":"Every row of `Q` strictly increases (left to right). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauAllLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauAllLt","kind":"def","line":886,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L886-L888","doc":"Every entry of the tableau `Q` is strictly `< s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_shape_eq_P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_shape_eq_P","kind":"theorem","line":868,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L868-L874","doc":"**`Q(w)` has the same shape as `P(w)`.**  The recording tableau matches the\ninsertion tableau cell-for-cell — the shape agreement the RSK bijection's\n`(P, Q)` pairing rests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec_fst","kind":"theorem","line":863,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L863-L866","doc":"`(insertWordRec w).1 = insertWord w`: the recording tableau's P-component is\nthe insertion tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_shape","kind":"theorem","line":851,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L851-L861","doc":"The recording fold keeps `P` and `Q` shape-aligned throughout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux_fst","kind":"theorem","line":842,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L842-L849","doc":"The P-component of the recording fold is exactly `insertWord`'s fold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRec","kind":"def","line":837,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L837-L840","doc":"The `P`/`Q` tableaux of a word: `P(w)` is the insertion tableau, `Q(w)` the\nrecording tableau (0-based step indices). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordRecAux","kind":"def","line":829,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L829-L835","doc":"Recording-aware word insertion: fold the letters of `w` left to right,\nthreading the P/Q tableaux and the step counter `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_shape","kind":"theorem","line":791,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L791-L827","doc":"**`insertRec` keeps `P` and `Q` shape-aligned.**  Given a shape-aligned\ninput (`tableauShape P = tableauShape Q`), the output tableaux still share a\nshape — a bump preserves every row length, an append/new-row grows both `P`\nand `Q` by one cell in the same row.  So `Q` tracks `P`'s Young-diagram shape\nexactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_fst_eq_insert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec_fst_eq_insert","kind":"theorem","line":776,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L776-L789","doc":"**The P-component of `insertRec` is exactly Schensted insertion.**  The\nrecording bookkeeping never perturbs the insertion tableau: `Q` and `s` only\nfill the Q-component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertRec","kind":"def","line":759,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L759-L774","doc":"**Combined P/Q insertion.**  Insert `x` into `P` by the Schensted cascade,\nwriting the step index `s` into the matching new cell of `Q`.  A bump leaves\nthe current row's Q-length unchanged and cascades to the next row; an append\nwrites `s` at the end of the Q-row; falling off the bottom starts a new `[s]`\nQ-row (mirroring the new `[x]` P-row).  `Q` is read via `headD`/`tail`; when\n`P` and `Q` are shape-aligned (the maintained invariant) these are the true\nhead row and tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_cons","kind":"theorem","line":756,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L756-L757","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape_nil","kind":"theorem","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L754-L754","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.tableauShape","kind":"def","line":751,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L751-L752","doc":"Row-length profile (shape) of a tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":722,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L722-L733","doc":"`insertWord w` is column-strict for every word `w`: the insertion tableau\n`P(w)` has strictly-increasing columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":678,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L678-L720","doc":"**The insertion cascade preserves column-strictness.**  `insert T x` keeps\na column-strict tableau column-strict: the no-bump case appends a cell past\nthe lower row (`strictBelow_append_upper`); the bump case lowers the upper\nentry and cascades the ejected value down, preserving every column\ncomparison by `strictBelow_bump_step`.  This is the last structural\ninvariant needed to make `P(w)` a semistandard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_tail","kind":"theorem","line":671,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L671-L676","doc":"`ColStrict` is inherited by the tail of the tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_bump_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_bump_step","kind":"theorem","line":591,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L591-L669","doc":"**The bumping lemma (single step).**  If `lower` sits strictly below `row`\n(`StrictBelow`) and `rowInsert row x` bumps `y`, then after `y` re-inserts\ninto `lower` the new upper row still sits strictly below the new lower row.\nThis is the structural heart of RSK column-strictness: the ejected `y > x`\nlands in `lower` at a column no further right than where `x` landed in\n`row`, so every column comparison is preserved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_headD_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_headD_eq","kind":"theorem","line":583,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L583-L589","doc":"The head row of `insert rest y` is the head row of `rest` after `rowInsert`\nwith `y` (reading the empty row when `rest = []`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":577,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L577-L581","doc":"The insertion cascade never yields the empty tableau (it always adds a cell). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_none_eq_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_none_eq_append","kind":"theorem","line":565,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L565-L575","doc":"A no-bump row insertion appends: the new row is exactly `r ++ [x]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_eq_getElem_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_eq_getElem_mem","kind":"theorem","line":560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L560-L563","doc":"In-range `getD` equals the plain indexed entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_set_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_set_ne","kind":"theorem","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L555-L558","doc":"`getD` away from the set index is unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_set_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_set_self","kind":"theorem","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L550-L553","doc":"`getD` at the set index reads the written value (index in range). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_set_smaller","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_set_smaller","kind":"theorem","line":518,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L518-L535","doc":"**Lowering an upper entry preserves `StrictBelow`**: replacing `upper[k]` by\na strictly smaller `x` keeps every column comparison (the changed column only\ngets smaller above).  This is the bump case's effect on the upper row\n(`rowInsert` writes `x < y` at the bump index). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_append_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_append_upper","kind":"theorem","line":506,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L506-L516","doc":"**Appending a cell to the upper row preserves `StrictBelow`**: the new column\nsits beyond `lower`, so existing comparisons are untouched.  (The no-bump /\nappend case of the cascade.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L503-L504","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_nil","kind":"theorem","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L501-L501","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ColStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.ColStrict","kind":"def","line":497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L497-L499","doc":"A tableau has strictly-increasing columns iff consecutive rows are\n`StrictBelow`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.StrictBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.StrictBelow","kind":"def","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L492-L495","doc":"`lower` sits strictly below `upper`: no longer, each entry strictly exceeds\nthe one directly above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.bump_findIdx_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.bump_findIdx_mono","kind":"theorem","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L463-L481","doc":"**Bump-column monotonicity** — the bumping lemma's heart.  If the value `y`\nbumped from `upper` (at `upper.findIdx (x < ·)`) sits at every column strictly\nbelow a larger entry of `lower` (column-strictness, `upper[j] < lower[j]`), then\n`y` re-inserts into `lower` at a column no further right:\n`lower.findIdx (y < ·) ≤ upper.findIdx (x < ·)`.  This is exactly why columns of\nthe insertion tableau stay strictly increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_le_of_lt_findIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_le_of_lt_findIdx","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L446-L461","doc":"**Entries strictly before the bump index are `≤ x`.**  `findIdx` is the\n*leftmost* entry `> x`, so everything to its left is `≤ x`.  This is what makes\nthe new-bottom-row cell (column `0`) sit strictly below a smaller entry when the\nbump came from a later column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.findIdx_le_of_getElem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.findIdx_le_of_getElem","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L425-L444","doc":"**`findIdx` upper bound.**  If the predicate holds at index `c`, the first\nindex where it holds is `≤ c`.  (General `List` fact; the monotonicity engine.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bump_getElem?","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bump_getElem?","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L397-L415","doc":"**The bumped value is exactly the old entry at the bump index.**  Completing\nthe positional picture: a bump reads off `r[findIdx]` (as `y`) and writes `x`\nthere.  Stated with `getElem?` to avoid threading the `< length` proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_findIdx_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_findIdx_lt","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L390-L395","doc":"**The bump position is valid** (`< row length`): there is an entry `> x`\n(the bumped one, `∈ r` and `> x`), so `findIdx` lands inside the row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bump_eq_set","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bump_eq_set","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L373-L388","doc":"**Positional characterization of a bump.**  When `rowInsert` bumps, the new\nrow is the old row with its leftmost entry `> x` (at `findIdx`) replaced by `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L357-L363","doc":"An inserted row is never empty (it always contains at least `x`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length_le","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L349-L355","doc":"Row insertion changes the length by `0` (a bump) or `+1` (an append) — never\nmore.  A structural bound the later Young-diagram *shape* reasoning consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_none_forall_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_none_forall_le","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L332-L347","doc":"**No bump ⟺ every entry is `≤ x`.**  When `rowInsert` appends (no bump), the\ninserted `x` is `≥` every entry of the row — so the append lands `x` as the new\nrow-maximum, the base case of the column-strictness cascade. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bumped_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bumped_mem","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L317-L330","doc":"**The bumped entry is a genuine entry of the original row.**  Together with\n`rowInsert_bumped_gt`, the value cascading downward is an old entry `> x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bumped_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_bumped_gt","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L302-L315","doc":"**The bumped entry is strictly greater than the inserted value.**  `rowInsert`\nbumps the *leftmost entry `> x`*, so whenever it returns `some y`, `x < y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_content","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L278-L290","doc":"`content (P(w)) = ↑w`: the insertion tableau of a word holds exactly the multiset of its\nletters — the content-preservation fact RSK's bijection content-matching rests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_content","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L258-L276","doc":"**The insertion cascade conserves entries**: `insert T x` holds exactly the entries of `T`\ntogether with `x`.  (The bumped value is never lost — it cascades down until appended.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_content","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L241-L256","doc":"**Row insertion conserves entries**: the new row plus the bumped value (if any) carries exactly\nthe old row's entries together with the inserted `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_cons","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L238-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content_nil","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L236-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.content","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L231-L234","doc":"The multiset of entries of a tableau (sum of its rows' multisets). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.bumpMs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.bumpMs","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L226-L229","doc":"The bumped value as a multiset (`∅` if no bump, `{a}` if `a` is bumped). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_totalCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_totalCells","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L210-L222","doc":"`|P(w)| = |w|`: the insertion tableau of a word has exactly as many cells as the word has\nletters — the cell-count fact RSK's cardinality argument rests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_totalCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_totalCells","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L196-L208","doc":"**Each insertion adds exactly one cell.**  A bump replaces an entry (no length change in that\nrow) but cascades the bumped value downward, which eventually appends one cell (or starts a new\nrow); a no-bump appends directly.  Either way the total grows by exactly one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.totalCells_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.totalCells_cons","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L193-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.totalCells_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.totalCells_nil","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L191-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.totalCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.totalCells","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L188-L189","doc":"Total number of cells of a tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length_some","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length_some","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L175-L186","doc":"A bumping row insertion keeps the row length fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length_none","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length_none","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L162-L173","doc":"A no-bump row insertion (append) grows the row by one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_rowsSorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_rowsSorted","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L148-L158","doc":"`insertWord w` has weakly-increasing rows, for every word `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_rowsSorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_rowsSorted","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L121-L146","doc":"**The cascade preserves row-sortedness.**  Each row that changes does so by `rowInsert`, which\nkeeps it weakly increasing (`rowInsert_sorted`); untouched rows are unchanged.  So `insert`\nmaps row-sorted tableaux to row-sorted tableaux — the invariant making `insertWord w` a tableau\nwith weakly-increasing rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowsSorted_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowsSorted_nil","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.RowsSorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.RowsSorted","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L116-L117","doc":"Every row of a tableau is weakly increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L112-L114","doc":"The insertion tableau `P(w)` of a word `w`: insert its letters left to right into the empty\ntableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L102-L110","doc":"**Schensted insertion into a tableau** (a `List (List ℕ)` of rows).  Row-insert `x` into the\nfirst row; if an entry is bumped, cascade the bumped value into the next row; if the cascade falls\noff the bottom, start a new one-cell row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L81-L98","doc":"**The inserted row stays weakly increasing.**  This is the structural invariant that keeps the\nRSK insertion tableau well-formed: bumping the leftmost entry `> x` by the smaller `x` preserves\nsortedness, and appending `x` past a row all `≤ x` does too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_length","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L66-L79","doc":"Row insertion either keeps the length (a bump) or increases it by one (an append). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_rowInsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_rowInsert","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L48-L64","doc":"Every entry of the inserted row is an old entry of `r` or the inserted value `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_cons","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L44-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_nil","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedInsertion.lean#L34-L40","doc":"**Schensted row insertion.** Insert `x` into a (weakly-increasing) row `r`: bump the leftmost\nentry `> x`, returning `(newRow, some bumped)`; if none, append `x`, returning `(r ++ [x], none)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}